# Testing Results and Project Outcomes

## Testing Performed

1. ESP32 board programming and initialization.
2. Hall Effect sensor pulse detection.
3. RPM measurement.
4. Wind speed calculation.
5. LCD display testing.

## Project Outcomes

- Successfully developed an ESP32-based wind speed measurement prototype.
- Measured anemometer RPM using Hall Effect sensor pulses.
- Calculated wind speed from sensor readings.
- Displayed real-time RPM and wind speed on a 16x2 I2C LCD.

## Current Project Status

The hardware prototype and LCD-based monitoring system are implemented.

Cloud connectivity and remote monitoring are planned as future enhancements.

## Applications

- Weather monitoring
- Wind energy systems
- Agricultural monitoring
- Environmental studies

## Future Improvements

- IoT cloud dashboard integration
- Wireless monitoring
